        "footnote_text": "Player look different? If yours has an on/off switch on the back,",
        "footnote_link": "see the fixes for our first players",
        "glance_heading": "All the lights at a glance",
        "test_heading": "Seeing a colour that isn't listed?",
        "test_text": "If the play button glows white, or changes colour and buzzes each time you press a button, the player is in a checking mode we use in our workshop. Nothing is wrong and nothing is harmed. Hold the play button until the player switches off and keep holding for about 30 seconds. Let go, wait 10 seconds, then switch it on again as normal.",
        "restart_anchor": "reset",
        "restart_heading": "Still stuck? Reset the player",
        "restart_intro": "<p>Only if nothing else has worked. A reset clears the places saved on the player, so every book starts again from the beginning. Your books and their stories aren't affected.</p>",
        "timeline_1": "0–3 s",
        "timeline_2": "Light goes off. Keep holding…",
        "timeline_3": "30 s: let go",
        "restart_steps": "<ol><li>Press and hold the play button.</li><li>After a few seconds the light goes off. <strong>Don't let go.</strong> Letting go here only switches it off.</li><li>Keep holding for 30 seconds in total, then let go.</li><li>Wait 10 seconds before switching it back on, so it starts first time.</li><li>Press play to switch it on. The button glows blue when it's ready.</li></ol>",
        "back_text": "Back to the player without a switch",
        "earlier_heading": "Our first players",
        "earlier_intro": "These players have an on/off switch on the back. Most problems come down to the switch, the charge or a dusty connector."
      }
